# Operator-facing planning docs that live next to source for ergonomic
# cross-reference but aren't part of the project's public history.
# Keep these in sync with the corresponding doc in their target repo
# (or the dedicated planning workspace) when content matters.
MAINNET_PLAN.md
BENCH_PLAN.md
BENCH_CONTRACTS.md
EXPLORER_PLAN.md
TESTNET_LAUNCH_TRACKER.md

# cargo-fuzz artefacts (task 053). Crate lives outside the workspace
# and has its own Cargo.lock + target/ dir + corpus dir which we don't
# commit. Fuzz crashes go into fuzz/artifacts/ and should also stay
# out of the repo — they can be MB-sized and reproduce from the seed.
fuzz/Cargo.lock
fuzz/target/
fuzz/corpus/
fuzz/artifacts/

# Generated testnet output directories from `pyde testnet`. These
# contain validator Falcon keys, threshold-encryption per-validator
# shares, and the faucet signing key — all operator-private. The
# two-laptop runbook (docs/two-laptop-soak.md) writes to
# `two-laptop-net/`; other ad-hoc runs use `net/` or `testnet/`.
two-laptop-net/
testnet/
net/
aws-*-net/

# Operator-private node-address topology files for cloud deployments.
# These contain real public IPs of validator instances and live next
# to the placeholder-only two-laptops.toml — never commit them.
crates/node/testdata/aws-*.toml

# Ad-hoc operator notes (IP lists, scratch files) under scripts/.
scripts/.txt
scripts/*.local

# macOS Finder metadata
.DS_Store
